    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan presents a genuinely balanced case that supports a Hold. The bull's structural case is sound \u2014 JPM trades 14.5% above a rising 200-day SMA ($163.56), holds above the 50-day SMA ($185.92), and has a fortress balance sheet ($4.09T assets, $336.6B equity, 8.2% equity ratio). However, the bear correctly identifies that the June 12 low of $182.79 is a LOWER low than the May 20 low of $186.66, contradicting the bull's \"higher low\" claim, and short-term momentum has rolled over (below 10-day EMA, negative MACD). Critically, the fundamental picture is incomplete \u2014 there is no income statement or macro/rate data available in this window, so earnings power and the rate environment cannot be confirmed. With the stock sitting mid-range ($182.79-$190.83), a lower low printed, and negative short-term momentum on one side versus an intact structural uptrend and fortress balance sheet on the other, neither side has a decisive edge. I will maintain existing positions at ~$187.35, not chase new longs at this price, and wait for either a confirmed breakout above $190.83 on volume or a pullback toward the $182.79 support zone before adding. Position sizing stays at neutral benchmark-weight.\n\n**Entry Price**: 187.35\n\n**Stop Loss**: 177.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral benchmark-weight allocation; do not overweight until technical breakout above $190.83 confirms or fundamental data becomes available.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
